A||||13||TRiAD||Anybody have these on their car?||||6||
Z||000000||TRiAD||12-27-2001||05:49 PM||||Well, I've seen these around, and fell in love with them. They're the "snake-eyes" lic plate LEDs. I bid on a pair of the blue ones, and will be installing them on the rear...I may nodify the hood and washer jets to use the blue LED washers on the front...<P><BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=599657113&r=0&t=0&showTutorial=0&ed=1009483403&indexURL=0&rd=1" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAP I.dll?ViewItem&item=599657113&r=0&t=0&showTutorial=0&ed=1009483403&indexURL=0&rd=1</A> <P>Please don't bother flaming me, I know it's goofy, but they'll be on their own switch, so I'll probably only use them when cruising with other Fieros or at a GTG.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://centralillinoisimports.org/uploads/files/SigRear4.gif">   <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Reality||12-27-2001||05:52 PM||||If they're on a switch I don't see where the problem would be. Can't be any goofier(?) than those neon license plate holders. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||12-27-2001||06:01 PM||||I like them for the fact that they're connected to the backup lights... and I've got Green LED Tireflys on my GT- so no flames from me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And for $10- it's all just fun anyway!  Might have to look into a set of those myself.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-27-2001||06:06 PM||||pretty cool, its your car, dont worry about what other ppl think.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||12-27-2001||06:44 PM||||Be careful about putting blue lights on the front of your car, some states don't take too kindly 'bout that.||||reg||1
Z||000005||CoolBlue87GT||12-27-2001||07:41 PM||||Here an idea, If you have a plastic tag frame, you can get a set of flashing bright blue led's from any RadioShack, and drill a small hole & install them.<P>They have red, orange, blue, green, and white. (white is the rarest)<P>Some blink, some are solid. Make sure you get 12v as there are many voltage's.<P>They have some chrome led holders that would make the job easy.<P>I've got a set of red ones mounted out on our mailbox. At night I can see them from 1/2 mile away ! I tell our friends to look for the blinking mailbox. (the set I used are 2.3v, hooked up w/two AA batt.)||||reg||6
Z||000006||TRiAD||12-27-2001||10:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B>Here an idea, If you have a plastic tag frame, you can get a set of flashing bright blue led's from any RadioShack, and drill a small hole & install them.<P>They have red, orange, blue, green, and white. (white is the rarest)<P>Some blink, some are solid. Make sure you get 12v as there are many voltage's.<P>They have some chrome led holders that would make the job easy.<P>I've got a set of red ones mounted out on our mailbox. At night I can see them from 1/2 mile away ! I tell our friends to look for the blinking mailbox. (the set I used are 2.3v, hooked up w/two AA batt.)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's cool!<P>These are the chrome bolts with blue LEDs, no flashing ones, and these will go on the rear only, the washer nozzle ones will go on the front. <P>Blue light of any kind is illegal in IL, but if it's a colored headlamp, cornerlamp, or similar, they don't seem to enforce it. But, like I said, these will have their own switch, so if I get pulled over, I can just turn them off on the street and use them only at shows and get togethers. <P>I expected someone to flame about these...nice to see I was wrong. <P>Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||12-27-2001||11:36 PM||||Cute!  I like the idea of hooking them to the backup lights (or their own switch is fine, like you said, just having FUN!)<P>The washer squirter lights... not my thing, I think they look silly, but I DO notice cars with them at night...  <P>Which was a major justification I used on my $600+ HID Xenon headlight conversion...<P>So hey!<P>Enjoy man!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||SHarperFieroGT||12-27-2001||11:49 PM||||I haev those exact neon lights on my GT!!<BR>They were such a pain to run the wires... at first i wanted to run a switch on my dash and run a power wire all the way back there but i got lazy and just threaded the wires through the license plate bolt holes up my bumper to where my PONTIAC lens thing is between my tailights, just spliced into the wire for that since it only comes on when my ignition is on.  I like the fact that i can never accidently leave them turned on, and i wouldn't wanna mount them on there if they were just gonna be on when i back up!!  thats why I have Green Back Up Bulbs... They look nice, But yea no tickets or being pulled over for them yet!!   <P>SHarper<BR>86 Red Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||12-27-2001||11:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B>....you can get a set of flashing bright blue led's from any RadioShack, and drill a small hole & install them.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Aren't flashing blue lights a K-Mart thing?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||johnt671||12-28-2001||08:46 AM||||I'd Check with the police/motor vehicle dept about all of those different color lights.  Someone posted about a guy that had different color lights all over the front and back of his car getting nailed by the police.  Around here different color lights are used to I.D. emergency cars.  Blue =police,red=fire and green=EMS.  A ricer here has blue lights in his defroster openings, and he'll be busted soon for impersonating a cop.  Not trying to flame or bust your chops, but check before you spend money on this.||||reg||1
Z||000011||falconhulk||12-28-2001||10:20 AM||||I have Neon Blue fog lights and have driven through PA, VA, Wva, MD, and Delaware.  Never had a cop stop me.  They ususally get upset when you change marker lights or headlights to non standard colors.  They dont seem to much care about accessory lighting.||||reg||1
